      en: [
        'BLOOD VOLUME IS THE SINGLE MOST IMPORTANT FACTOR: Inoculating 10 mL per bottle in 2-3 sets (40-60 mL total) achieves >99% detection sensitivity.',
        'CoNS, diphtheroids, or P. acnes in a single bottle indicates pseudobacteremia; multiple positive bottles in a patient with a catheter indicate true CRBSI.',
        'Optimal blood-to-broth ratio is 1:5 to 1:10 to dilute host inhibitory serum bactericidal factors.',
        'SPS is the only recommended anticoagulant; Heparin, EDTA, and Citrate inhibit bacterial growth.',
        'Routine automated incubation of 5 days is sufficient for common pathogens; extended incubation is needed for Brucella, Bartonella, and systemic dimorphic fungi.'
      ]
